 $3.$ This occurs when $x\\to -\\infty .$ However, note that this point is not included in the graph.\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $-1$ and $3,$ not including $-1$ and $3.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $-1<y<3,$ which can also be written as $-1<f(x)<3.$"} :step/id #uuid "aba196a5-a956-50e2-b8a6-61106b7dc46b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489316}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489362 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489195 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "151cd673-35b1-5901-b1e4-3f2f71811a31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488517}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488517} :answer-field/id #uuid "af246519-227d-5a39-92f0-c9fb3022be21" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489113} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c165e391-96c0-5f1a-8559-109c7f748bfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488861}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488861} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4799eb0-92e5-5e8a-a05b-b1fc23cc5f4d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489116} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59ae91eb-e7d1-5b05-ab82-7c77711c0e9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488641}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488641} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbbd8104-f926-5b39-b3f0-4089b321c8ec" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2636e2eb-9d96-5c30-898f-0b55c9dd4bbf" :question/math-academy-id "q-236386" :question/problem "![](images/20/20cf8d018f748534720eb3efe21c4adf9354a015d824dcc15bfd9c33ad14a895.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?\n\nThe range is \n{{field-1}}\n$<f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the smallest and largest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- The smallest $y$-value is $1.$ This occurs when $x\\to -\\infty .$ However, note  that this point is not included in the graph.\n\n- There is no largest $y$-value.\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $1$ and $\\infty ,$ but not including $1.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $1<y<\\infty ,$ which can also be written as \n$1<f(x)<\\infty .$"} :step/id #uuid "ceb88876-37e1-5b22-af2a-9cf0a535596a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489363}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489363 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489242 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e1d5456-f9d4-5149-86a2-9ba9a7c28a31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488725}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488725} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b650656-bd36-5828-a479-5f52c0e48b4b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489058} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2520b781-4fa8-5f19-abe9-c773ef419534" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488546}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488546} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b7ed819-da82-5a1b-a80b-815d82f58698" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489067} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "273427b6-1181-5cc4-9482-efd6c25dd700" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488554}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488554} :answer-field/id #uuid "7167fd1b-94c1-5af4-adca-6b79f3ab33a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489074}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "92babace-3fcf-5d4a-8789-c7e1f3a12026" :question/math-academy-id "q-236716" :question/problem "![](images/6a/6a837faad775bb111760b2e90920c0490c42473c77f74f8be7a46271df154d97.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?\n\nThe range is \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$f(x)<$\n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "We find the ranges of the individual pieces and then calculate their union:\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in (-3,1)$ is $(-1,3)$\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in [1,4)$ is $\\{1\\}$\n\nTherefore, the range of $f(x)$ is $(-1,3)\\cup \\{1\\}=(-1,3),$ which can also be written as \n\n$$\n-1<f(x)<3.\n$$\n\n**Note:** From the graph, we see that the values $y=-1$ and $y=3$ are NOT valid outputs of the function $y=f(x).$ Therefore, we use \"less than\" $(<)$ instead of \"less than or equal to\" $(\\le )$ at these endpoints."} :step/id #uuid "cf6a1dfd-5754-5ce6-84a6-e24b8966c20d"}] :activity/title "The Range of a Function: Advanced Cases" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488449}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490353} :activity/id #uuid "a4407aef-3121-52a9-b946-f3e8ebff0a98" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050580 :topic/id #uuid "557f8b58-be49-555e-8162-3d1448eaff0c" :topic/math-academy-id 3728} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490330 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490222 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "077fd3b6-a66f-5992-89ff-f734285036e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1<f(x)<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489533} {:answer/id #uuid "7bd4f26c-68d7-508b-ae68-df55769b27e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\infty <f(x)<1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489797} {:answer/id #uuid "85a2736a-d41e-5e05-9a88-0d47451e0a05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1<f(x)<\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489820} {:answer/id #uuid "a7ab8a0a-f5d1-5b79-8ad9-de72a82f973b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\infty <f(x)\\le 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489884} {:answer/id #uuid "c20f2f3c-997e-5379-8c75-90a1c8d674a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1\\le f(x)<\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489935}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489797} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7dd7694-ccde-505f-9224-5e793348c4a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490197}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "24be045a-a1e0-562b-a001-f17a0f6f12b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-79997" :question/problem "![](images/ac/acbf4ae592e7912e6e27415ce99f872c4c0ec1737cfa3269635f37f7fa0fe5db.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the smallest and largest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- There is no smallest $y$-value.\n\n- The largest $y$-value is $1.$ This occurs when $x\\to -\\infty .$ However, note that this point is not included in the graph.\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $-\\infty $ and $1,$ but not including $1.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $-\\infty <y<1,$ which can also be written as  $-\\infty <f(x)<1.$"} :step/id #uuid "027ab44b-48d6-5961-8e71-f93826f26196" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490379}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490348 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490228 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3e2fe1e-5ce8-5259-883a-e27ba55b0ebc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489908}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489908} :answer-field/id #uuid "2356dd8e-95af-53aa-99c1-588dd0a4fe73" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490089} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42a84cca-e35f-5c4a-b07e-845a7d28433f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489667}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489667} :answer-field/id #uuid "3443567b-7d91-5f03-9d4e-6b2b217a9066" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490103} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80e903e5-f2b3-5ed4-a09b-70f4dda6a048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489807}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489807} :answer-field/id #uuid "9abeb5f8-371d-515e-a1f6-7daf65af6f1e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490163}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2c426db9-03a0-51ed-9522-bdc02ff647af" :question/math-academy-id "q-236388" :question/problem "![](images/49/49288e2c082854cfc27a2d48af2d82a96016a3c1394066471d49873e4c75878e.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?\n\nThe range is \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$f(x)<$\n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the smallest and largest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- The smallest $y$-value is $1.$ This occurs when $x=0.$\n\n- There is no largest $y$-value.\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $1$ and $\\infty ,$ including $1.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $1\\le y<\\infty ,$ which can also be written as \n$1\\le f(x)<\\infty .$"} :step/id #uuid "356e531e-4a8b-5a5a-96af-77c558013231" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490375}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490353 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490278 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39cc2ab9-0e69-5e63-9804-2b53b2eb63cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[-2,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489645} {:answer/id #uuid "5825da